(7641562, 1240779, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SandyP:</b></div><hr/><i> I love this photo, Roz!  I have always loved welding photos with the sparkly light and edgy subject matter!  Your amazing making something like this so artful! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thankyou so much Sandy .. a comment when you''re on the second page after voting rolls over is a great thing to get .. and thankyou .. xx</td>', 'Originally posted by SandyP: I love this photo, Roz!  I have always loved welding photos with the sparkly light and edgy subject matter!  Your amazing making something like this so artful!   thankyou so much Sandy .. a comment when you''re on the second page after voting rolls over is a great thing to get .. and thankyou .. xx', '2019-09-16 17:18:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7641563, 1240640, 30049, '<td valign="top">FWIW - Had this tied for my top pick (I gave out two 9''s).  Glad to see it made the Top Ten - worthy of much more IMO.<br/> <br/>The processing and macro aspect make this a very unique image.  Could be a pair of elephant trunks, or some very well used knees, perhaps even a pair of fingers on a hand.  :-P  Nice.</td>', 'FWIW - Had this tied for my top pick (I gave out two 9''s).  Glad to see it made the Top Ten - worthy of much more IMO. The processing and macro aspect make this a very unique image.  Could be a pair of elephant trunks, or some very well used knees, perhaps even a pair of fingers on a hand.  :-P  Nice.', '2019-09-16 17:22:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7641564, 1240815, 30049, '<td valign="top">FWIW - Had this tied for my top pick (I gave out two 9''s).  I really this abstract image, and have tilted my head both ways to see if it played any better with a different perspective - nope, it plays just fine this way!  Great detail and just enough side light.  Only nit that could have held it back some is it gets a bit softer near the bottom edge.  A square crop perhaps to lose that?  Bah.  Just speculating.  It is what it is, and I liked it.  Well done.</td>', 'FWIW - Had this tied for my top pick (I gave out two 9''s).  I really this abstract image, and have tilted my head both ways to see if it played any better with a different perspective - nope, it plays just fine this way!  Great detail and just enough side light.  Only nit that could have held it back some is it gets a bit softer near the bottom edge.  A square crop perhaps to lose that?  Bah.  Just speculating.  It is what it is, and I liked it.  Well done.', '2019-09-16 17:25:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7641565, 1240802, 30049, '<td valign="top">This was in my Top 3 - gave it an 8.  The shadows with the B&amp;W presentation sold it for me.  Just enough left out of the frame to keep it edgy.  Well done.</td>', 'This was in my Top 3 - gave it an 8.  The shadows with the B&W presentation sold it for me.  Just enough left out of the frame to keep it edgy.  Well done.', '2019-09-16 17:27:44.000000', NULL, 0),
